<title>UK: UK April net consumer credit up 691 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK April net consumer credit up 691 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK consumer credit grew by a net seasonally adjusted 691 million stg in April after a 793 million stg increase in March, Bank of England data showed.  </p>
<p>The Bank of England released the following data -</p>
<p>NET LENDING (previously released data in brackets, in MLN STG)</p>
<p>					     April   March	    APR,96</p>
<p> Total net lending		     2,494   2,626 (2,550)  2,530</p>
<p>  -- Consumer credit		   691     793   (780)    1,215</p>
<p>  -- Secured on dwellings	    1,803   1,833 (1,770)  1,314</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN of net consumer lending BY SOURCE -</p>
<p>  -- Banks				 578    588    (570)    983</p>
<p>  -- Building societies		 19	7     (8)	36</p>
<p>  -- Retailers			     3     43    (44)	13</p>
<p>  -- Credit card			 126    210    (205)    351</p>
<p>CONSUMER CREDIT (seasonally adjusted, in PCT)</p>
<p> Total personal borrowing mth/mth  0.5    0.5   (0.5)     0.5</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;	  &quot;     yr/yr    6.9    6.9   (6.9)     5.4</p>
<p> Consumer credit mth/mth	     0.9    1.0   (1.0)     1.8</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;     yr/yr		 16.5   17.5  (17.1)    14.6</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
